@baseUrl = https://localhost:7179
@adminEmail = admin@flyreservation.local
# Type your AdminUser:Password (user secrets) here while testing. Do not commit it
@adminPassword = CHANGE_ME

### AUTH) Login as admin. Send this first: the admin requests below read the token from its response
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}


### 1) List all reservations
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 2) Create reservation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "flightId": 3,
  "passengerId": 3
}

### 7) Deney 17-E: same key twice → same PNR (click Send twice)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: deney-17-1

{
  "flightId": 2,
  "passengerId": 4
}

### 3) Get reservation by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/2

### 4) Cancel reservation
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/6

### 5) Deney B2: try to set server-side fields from client (DTO should ignore them)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "flightId": 1,
  "passengerId": 1,
  "pnrCode": "HACK01",
  "createdAt": "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "id": 999
}

### 6) Deney B3: reservation for a non-existent flight
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "flightId": 9999,
  "passengerId": 1
}

### Pay a reservation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/1/payment
